// Frame inspection for input/regression/part-combine-relative.ly (session 129, not a twin).
// The book's claim is about SCOPE: an outer \relative is ignored by \partCombine, an inner one
// is not. Question asked here: can Lily# put an octave mode INSIDE one part's music, so that
// the "inner" half of the claim can be written at all?
octave absolute
time 4/4

part vone { clef treble }
part vtwo { clef treble }

section A {
  vone { octave relative e'2 f | }
  vtwo { octave relative c'2 d | }
}

form main { ~A }

score main { combinedStaff { vone vtwo } }
